Raisse the Thaumaturge <raisse@valdyas.org> writes:
> Some experimentation in explore mode seems to suggest that if you're a
> <race><role> you can never polymorph into a <race><monster>; I started
> a game as a gnomish healer, tried to poly into a gnome lord, a gnome
> king, a gnomish wizard and a plain gnome several times, but kept
> feeling like a new gnome.
> 
> Is this in fact true, or just a fluke of the RNG?

It is true. You can't polymorph into a monster that counts as being
part of your race, even if other races could polymorph into it; so, an
orc can't polyself into a goblin, for example, and a human can't
polyself into a Keystone Kop. Attempting to do so raises the 20%
chance of "You feel like a new <race>" to 100%.

